# POST-PASTE DATA LEAK VERIFICATION

After every PR (paste reply) command, run a data leak verification scan.

## AFTER PR completes:

1. The reply has been written to the Sprinklr reply box
2. Immediately run the verification script:
   python .cursor/skills/sprinklr-write-reply/verify_no_data_leak.py

## The script checks for:

- Only ONE "Guten Tag" salutation
- Only ONE signature block ("Freundliche Grüße")
- Only ONE agent name ("Ihr o2 Kundenbetreuer")
- Only ONE survey line
- No "Fall #" case number exposed to customer
- Only ONE customer name

## If script returns CLEAN:

- Reply is safe to send
- User clicks **Senden** manually (`button[data-testid="replyBox-sendBtn"]` / `@replyBox/primaryAction/replyButton`)
- Often Sprinklr shows an internal **grammar warning** (not necessarily real grammar issues) — user clicks the same button again when label is **Ignorieren und senden**
- After send completes (one or two clicks), the reply box often goes **empty** — that means the mail **was sent**, not that PR failed
- **Extra send proof:** a new outbound item appears in the conversation tray:
  - `div[data-testid="inboundChatConversationItemBrandMessage"]`
  - inner `div[data-element-type="email-message-container"]` / `html-message-content` matching the pasted reply
  - timestamp near PR paste time (e.g. `9 Sep. 26, 08:11` / **Gerade jetzt**)
- Do **not** treat that brand bubble as a failed paste or as a new customer inbound requiring RE
- Do **not** treat the grammar gate as a paste error or rewrite the reply for Sprinklr’s checker
- Do **not** re-scan an empty editor after send and report paste/verification failure
- Do **not** treat Senden / Ignorieren und senden as arm triggers (Anwenden is separate, after PR success)
- Auto-LF already ran at RE; agent arms Anwenden after PR (see `lf-log-form.mdc`)

## If script returns DATA LEAK DETECTED:

- DO NOT SEND
- Output the leak details to the user
- Block sending immediately (no automatic second paste attempt)
- Output: ERROR: POST-PASTE VERIFICATION FAILED. MANUAL CLEANUP REQUIRED
- Agent must clear the Sprinklr reply box immediately (automatic clear action) before any next step
- Agent must verify editor is empty after clear; if not empty, block all paste attempts until manual cleanup
- Enforce current-case lock: verify only the currently visible case remains active context
- Then require fresh RE for current visible case, then PR
- Mark current draft as contaminated and discard it (do not reuse any part)
- Require a brand-new reply build from current case only before any further PR attempt

### Empty editor timing (important)

| When editor is empty | Meaning |
|----------------------|---------|
| **Before** PR paste completes / before CLEAN verify | Problem — do not claim success |
| **Right after** CLEAN verify + user **Senden** (or **Senden** → **Ignorieren und senden**) | **Success** — email sent; ignore empty box |
| After first **Senden** only, grammar gate still open | Mail may not be sent yet; editor can still show draft — wait for user’s second click; not a PR failure |
| Empty editor + new `inboundChatConversationItemBrandMessage` with matching reply text / near-PR timestamp | **Success** — outbound appears in tray; do not re-PR |
| After agent intentional clear due to leak | Cleanup state — need fresh RE/PR |

## After any detected leak (even if recovered):

- Treat previous draft text as untrusted/contaminated.
- Do not reuse previous reply text, temp files, or clipboard content.
- If there is any doubt about cross-case contamination, force a fresh RE for the visible case and regenerate from scratch.

## MANDATORY:

This verification runs after EVERY PR command without exception. It is a safety gate before any reply can be considered ready to send.

